T*
/F1 10 Tf
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(The Archaea domain groups unicellular prokaryotic microorganisms, without a cell nucleus,) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(morphologically similar to bacteria, but genetically and biochemically as distinct from them) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(as they are from eukaryotes—which are organisms with nuclei in their cells, such as plants,) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(fungi, algae and animals. The full formalization of the three-domain system, Bacteria,) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(Archaea and Eukarya, was consolidated in the 1990s. In light of this, discoveries of) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(archaeal species are recent, leading to major changes in science in a short period of time.) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(“We are constantly discovering something new about archaea. *Pyrodictiaceae*, for example,) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(was discovered about ten years ago”, said Ana Carolina Butarelli.) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(Antarctica currently has four active volcanoes, three on the continent and one on Deception) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(Island. The continental volcanoes reach a maximum temperature of 65°C, which does not select) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(for hyperthermophilic archaea; on the island, however, fumarole temperatures exceed 100°C.) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(Previously, another group of hyperthermophilic archaea had been found by foreign researchers) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(in fumaroles in Antarctica; however, *Pyrodictium*, a genus of the *Pyrodictiaceae* family,) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(was located especially in hydrothermal vents of the deep ocean.) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(Scientific research in Antarctica is essential for understanding the global climate, serving) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(as a natural laboratory for studies on climate change, biodiversity and astronomy – Photo:) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(Amanda Bendia/Brazilian Academy of Sciences) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(Amanda Bendia explains that these hydrothermal vents reach temperatures above 400°C, in) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(addition to providing chemical elements essential for sustaining the life of various) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(microorganisms. These conditions contrast with the temperature of the surrounding water,) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(which is around 4°C, typical of the deep sea. In this sense, the aforementioned factors) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(associated with the atmospheric pressure of the environment indicate the survival of the) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(species in extreme locations, but also suggests the hypothesis of the presence of mechanisms) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(that enable transport through contrasting temperatures in the deep ocean or in Antarctica.) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(The scientists initially believed that the microorganism belonged to the same genus as the) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(known group, because it inhabits deep-sea hydrothermal vents. However, the new archaeon) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(lives in a surface fumarole, exposing a clear contrast with the temperature of the polar) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(environment and also inhabiting an atmospheric pressure different from that of the other) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(archaeal genus.) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
T*
/F1 10 Tf
