(## Genomics and adaptations) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(To clearly identify the differences between these microorganisms, in order to classify a new) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(genus and species, it is necessary to work with a protocol that addresses phylogeny,) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(molecular adaptations, comparative genomics and the functions performed by these beings.) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(Since it is not possible to cultivate them in the laboratory, due to the structural) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(difficulty of simulating the organisms’ living conditions, it is essential that the) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(extracted genome be of the highest possible quality, with less than 10% contamination in the) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(samples.) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(When working with genes recovered from an environmental sample, existing similarities in) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(their composition are analyzed in order to indicate the phylogenetic relationship between) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(the groups. This analysis can also indicate the metabolic activity of these beings, making) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(it possible to infer their behaviors.) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(“When we access the genome, we have access to a snapshot of the genetic material, but we do) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(not know whether that organism is actually transcribing and translating that material to) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(produce a protein. However, we can infer that it has this ability, since that gene is within) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(its genome”, noted Ana Carolina Butarelli.) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(Ana Carolina Butarelli - Photo: Lattes Curriculum) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(In addition, the characteristics identified in this genetic material demonstrate the) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(adaptations of the molecules to their natural habitat. Proteins play a crucial role in the) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(cell, acting as functional and structural agents, and it is possible to detect a) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(phylogenetic relationship based on protein composition. *Pyroantarcticum pellizari*, the) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(species discovered in the study, for example, has reverse gyrase – a protein that protects) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(DNA from denaturing, that is, from having its strands separated at high temperatures – a) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(common characteristic in hyperthermophilic archaea.) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(The analysis of unique genes in the newly assembled genome revealed a set of functionally) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(distinct elements, including pathways for sulfur and nitrogen cycling, together with) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(structural characteristics such as cannulae and stress-resistance systems, pointing to a) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(survival strategy adapted to transient energy availability, metal stress and interactions at) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(the community level in sediments. In this context, this genome offers an important overview) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(of the potential of microbial life to thrive in multiple extremes, a topic that is) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(increasingly relevant to studies in astrobiology, microbial bioprospecting and the impacts) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(of climate change on polar ecosystems.) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(“When dealing with an organism that is not widely studied, or in our case, a new genus and) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(species, having the complete genome directly affects the amount of information available) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(about that organism. Therefore, the 97% genome purity rate is an important path for) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(disseminating the discovery worldwide, as well as contributing to scientific databases”,) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(highlighted Francielli Peres.) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(Achieving a high genome purity rate was not an easy task for the researchers, who took about) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(a year to recover the DNA from the collected sample. In addition to the logistical obstacles) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(of research on Deception Island, Francielli Peres said that the small number of studies) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(available makes it difficult to gather information on the microorganisms. Laboratory and) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(computational analyses were also obstacles, as they required major University infrastructure) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(as well as the scientists’ expertise. “Although our work may seem very glamorous, cool and) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(incredible, there is also the complex side of being a scientist. Studying an organism that) Tj
